CHOWN(8)                   System Administration                    CHOWN(8)

NAME
    chown - give a file to another account

SYNOPSIS
    chown UID[:GID] PATH

DESCRIPTION
    Make account UID the owner of PATH, and GID its group if one is given.
    Both are numbers; there is no lookup by name. With no GID the file
    keeps its group: the shell reads it back and writes it again, because
    the operation sets both and an unspecified group would become 0.

THROUGH A CAPABILITY
    In a session chown stores nothing, and succeeds only to your own uid
    and group: a file is not given away through a capability.

SECURITY
    Without a session, the administrator only. Changing a mode and giving
    a file away are different acts with different rules: an owner may do
    the first, and only the administrator the second. The fs_server
    decides, against the identity the kernel attests.

SEE ALSO
    chmod(1), stat(1)
